cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "bfslib: a zero-allocation Swift CSR graph BFS for Apple Silicon"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Matevosyan
    given-names: Norayr
year: 2026
license: MIT
abstract: >
  bfslib is a single C-callable BFS function exposed from a Swift dynamic
  library, with a Python ctypes wrapper. It traverses Compressed Sparse
  Row contact graphs at ~4 ns/edge on Apple Silicon, completing a
  313 236-atom HIV-1 capsid BFS in 6 ms on an M5 Max. Designed for
  graph-traversal-bottlenecked workloads on biological structures at
  scales where standard normal-mode libraries hit memory walls.
  Amateur engineering project; no competitive claims beyond the measured
  numbers in the repository.
keywords:
  - graph
  - BFS
  - CSR
  - apple-silicon
  - biomolecular
  - GNN
  - bioinformatics
